# Document collections

A document collection groups related material under meaningful sections for a particular task or audience. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/document-collections/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use this structure for manuals, maintenance guidance or release documentation. Give the collection a focused title and short description. Group by the household task or equipment family rather than by storage format. Provide enough item context to distinguish similar titles.

## Structure and behaviour

Each group has a heading and a list of document links. Use a contents list when several groups make the page long. Add format and revision metadata at item level where relevant. Preserve a route from each document to its collection without implying it belongs to only one collection.

## Home Assistant boundary

This template does not upload private documents or subscribe users to updates. Only expose material intended for the current audience. A missing document must not be replaced with a clickable placeholder, and the collection must not advertise a downloadable bundle that has not been built.

